From: yinjiayi <yinjiayi@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] whirlpoolsum: terminate the digest buffer within its allocation

The check-mode buffer has DIGESTBYTES * 2 + 1 bytes. After encoding
DIGESTBYTES bytes, digest_ptr points at its last byte. Writing one byte
beyond that pointer is out of bounds. Terminate at digest_ptr instead.
The checksum comparison, error exit and original API tests are unchanged.

Source: review of official v1.1 src/whirlpoolsum.c
Upstream-Status: Not submitted (no upstream writes authorized)
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
--- a/src/whirlpoolsum.c
+++ b/src/whirlpoolsum.c
@@ -285 +285 @@
-			*(digest_ptr + 1) = '\0';
+			*digest_ptr = '\0';
